/*
  core/stressors/additive_load.spthy -- f_U for ADDITIVE cognitive load (V3 §2c), CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC.

  Cognitive Load Theory (Sweller 1988) is ADDITIVE: total load = intrinsic + extraneous + germane.
  A single step may sit BELOW the overload threshold, yet two moderate demands PRESENTED TOGETHER
  sum past it. The lookup detectors (sigma1/sigma3/sigma6) fire only on a step the lexicon rates at
  the 'hi' threshold (via !AtLeast, V3 §2a); this detector captures the case they miss -- TWO
  distinct steps each rated 'med' (individually sub-threshold), whose loads add to an overload.

  It reads only Layer-1 prompts + the Layer-2 demand levels, like every other detector:
    * two distinct !Step(P, _, _) for the SAME party
    * each with SOME demand dimension rated 'med' (the sub-threshold band: 'lo' < 'med' < 'hi')
  and, like the density detectors (sigma8/sigma9/sigma2-concurrent), it counts POSED prompts (no
  arithmetic -- Tamarin has no native sum over public constants; "two 'med' contributions present"
  IS the additive model). At onset it emits SetMask(P,'Busy') -- the same overload mask sigma1 would
  set from a single 'hi' step. !StressEnable(P) gates per party; InequalityAdditive is this file's
  private distinctness restriction; OnceAdditiveLoad bounds the onset per party.

  Contrast a profile can prove: with two 'med' steps and NO 'hi' step, sigma1 (HighCognitiveLoad)
  never onsets (nothing crosses 'hi' alone) yet AdditiveLoad DOES -- the moderate loads the
  single-step detector is blind to, summed.
*/

rule Trigger_AdditiveLoad [color=#eb5757]:
    [ !Step(P, s1, a1), !Demands(a1, dim1, 'med'),
      !Step(P, s2, a2), !Demands(a2, dim2, 'med'),
      !StressEnable(P) ]
  --[ AdditiveLoad(P), NeqAdd(s1, s2), SetMask(P,'Busy') ]->
    [ ]

restriction InequalityAdditive:
  "All x #i. NeqAdd(x,x)@i ==> F"

restriction OnceAdditiveLoad:
  "All p #i #j. AdditiveLoad(p)@i & AdditiveLoad(p)@j ==> #i = #j"
